WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.280
Most of what the SCP Foundation contains are&nbsp;
things you would rightfully prefer to keep&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:13.760
locked up. After all, not many people want to be&nbsp;
torn to shreds by SCP-096, tortured by SCP-106,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:20.640
eaten by SCP-082, or driven mad by the&nbsp;
sheer power and evil of the Scarlet King.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:26.160
Most SCPs are so cruel or dangerous that a run&nbsp;
in with even a cute little teddy bear could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:32.000
spell your doom. But what about the other side&nbsp;
of the coin? What about the SCP objects you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:39.840
don’t just want to avoid, but actually have&nbsp;
in your possession? To use as you see fit?

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:46.400
That, my friends, is exactly what we’re here to&nbsp;
discuss today: The SCP Objects you’d actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:52.880
want. No hidden catches, no nightmarish side&nbsp;
effects, no curses or strings attached. Think&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:59.520
of it almost like an anomalous skymall catalogue -&nbsp;
these are all the SCPs you never knew you wanted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.800
but would happily break into an SCP&nbsp;
Foundation containment facility to obtain.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.280
Speaking of breaking into places, let’s&nbsp;
start our odyssey of desirable anomalies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:15.520
with SCP-005. Have you ever forgotten or lost&nbsp;
your keys and been locked out of your house?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:21.120
Or maybe you’ve wanted to get a backstage pass&nbsp;
to your favorite concert without spending a dime?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:26.560
Heck, ever wanted to rob a bank or steal a million&nbsp;
dollars in gold from Fort Knox? Don’t worry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:32.160
we’re not here to judge, in fact, we’re going&nbsp;
to tell you how to make those dreams come true.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:38.400
What you need is The Skeleton Key. As you can&nbsp;
probably tell from the name, the skeleton key&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.720
is a normal, if a little old-fashioned-looking&nbsp;
key that can open literally any lock on earth.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:50.960
The White House? No problem. The Pentagon? Piece&nbsp;
of cake! Buckingham Palace? You can stroll right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:55.840
in and try on all the Queen’s finest jewelry.&nbsp;
Though of course, if you have no interest in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:02:01.120
becoming a master infiltrator and instead just&nbsp;
want a little more convenience in your daily life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.120 --> 00:02:06.640
the Skeleton Key also makes life easier by&nbsp;
making you only need one key for your house,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:09.920
your car, your bike lock, any lock at all!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:14.880
Think of all the pocket space you’ll&nbsp;
save, the possibilities are endless!

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:19.360
Speaking of “endless”, the next item on the&nbsp;
list gives a whole new meaning to the phrase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.760
“all you can eat.” Are you feeling&nbsp;
hungry? Are you part of the strong 95%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:29.840
of the human population that loves pizza?&nbsp;
Then buddy, you’re going to love SCP-458,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:36.000
also known as The Limitless Pizza Box. If the&nbsp;
name alone hasn’t sold you, then trust us,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.920
it’s going to get even more appealing. The anomaly&nbsp;
is a large-sized pizza takeout box from the Little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:47.440
Caesar’s pizza chain, and not only can this&nbsp;
box produce a truly endless quantity of pizza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.840
it also has an intuitive psychic&nbsp;
connection with whoever is using it.&nbsp;

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.120
Are you a devotee of Chicago-style deep dish?&nbsp;
You got it! Do you prefer more of a cheesy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:02.400
New York style slice with a little parmesan&nbsp;
sprinkled on top? Order up! Or maybe you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:08.720
a real traditionalist, and like it pure Italian -&nbsp;
no cheese, with a sprinkling of olives. Paisano,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:15.760
this box has got you covered. If you love pizza,&nbsp;
then SCP-458 is a must-have for your kitchen.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:22.000
So let’s say, hypothetically, you’ve just eaten&nbsp;
six pepperoni pizzas from SCP-458. Dishes are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.880
piled high in the sink, and you know they need&nbsp;
to be cleaned, but you’re in too much of a food&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.240
coma to get up and do anything. If only you could&nbsp;
just ring a little bell, and summon someone who’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:38.160
happily do all those stupid chores for you.&nbsp;
But alas, such a thing is impossible, right?

00:03:38.160 --> 00:03:45.040
Well you’ll be delighted to learn that this is&nbsp;
very much possible with SCP-662, also known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.400
the Butler’s Hand Bell. With a simple little ring,&nbsp;
you’ll summon the hyper-helpful British butler Mr.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:56.880
Deeds, an entity who literally lives to serve.&nbsp;
From doing your laundry to giving you foot rubs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.160
to assassinating that one jerk at your office who&nbsp;
always steals your pudding cups from the fridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:07.920
Mr. Deeds will endeavor to complete almost any&nbsp;
request within the realms of physical possibility.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.800
If you’ve ever wanted to lie back&nbsp;
and have someone else take care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:15.840
of all those pesky responsibilities that&nbsp;
make up the big to-do list that is life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.560
then SCP-662 is your must-have&nbsp;
anomalous ticket to freedom.

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:24.240
But maybe you don’t need a supernatural&nbsp;
butler to do everything for you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:28.960
You’re self sufficient, you take pride in&nbsp;
doing things for yourself. But you feel a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.960 --> 00:04:33.440
little down, and you could really use some&nbsp;
encouragement from someone close to you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:37.840
It’s times like these when you could really&nbsp;
use a few words from the father who is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:42.240
longer in your life to get you feeling&nbsp;
confident again. If this applies to you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:49.440
then you’ll definitely want to get your hands&nbsp;
on SCP-348, also known as A Gift From Dad.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:55.120
This wholesome soup bowl appears to be a spiritual&nbsp;
conduit to a loving fatherly figure, producing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.120 --> 00:05:00.160
the ultimate comfort food that will cure minor&nbsp;
ailments and leave you with a sense of happiness&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.840
and peace. Its effects may not be as amazing as&nbsp;
some of the other big ticket items on this list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:09.280
but it’s definitely one of the most&nbsp;
feel-good SCP objects out there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:12.960
and sure would be nice to have on&nbsp;
hand for the days when you need it.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.240
Speaking of feeling good, what feels better than&nbsp;
being in love - especially when the person you’re&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:23.600
in love with is just perfect for you, and&nbsp;
loves you back just as much? The problem is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:29.600
in a world as big and complicated as ours, who&nbsp;
knows where your true love is waiting to be found?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.600 --> 00:05:36.880
If you can feel yourself longing for the love of&nbsp;
your life, then you need SCP-2203, also known as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:42.640
Find the Right One for You. This device is a&nbsp;
standard “love tester” machine, the kind that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:49.440
were a lot more common in bars a couple decades&nbsp;
ago. But this is a love tester unlike any other.&nbsp;

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:54.800
When you use the machine, it doesn’t give you a&nbsp;
rating from “cold fish” to “casanova”. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:06:00.720
it dispenses a small card with a name and address&nbsp;
on it - which just so happens to be the name and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:06.480
address of your true love. It even features advice&nbsp;
on how to initially approach and woo the potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.480 --> 00:06:12.080
person of your dreams. For the socially awkward&nbsp;
and hopelessly romantic, this machine feels&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:17.760
heaven-sent. Just remember, once you’re actually&nbsp;
in the relationship, it’s up to you to be a good&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:23.680
partner if you want to make it last - SCP-2203&nbsp;
can’t help you with that part, we’re afraid.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:28.800
Of course, an important part of being a romantic&nbsp;
partner, or even just a good friend, is being&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.080
attentive to the other person’s needs. But to&nbsp;
meet those needs, you first need to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:38.560
them - and wouldn’t it be great to know someone’s&nbsp;
deepest desires without having to go through the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:46.560
trouble of actually asking? Allow us to introduce&nbsp;
you to SCP-978, also known as the Desire Camera!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:52.320
This simple polaroid camera allows the user to&nbsp;
peer into the very hearts of their subjects.

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.880
All you need to do is take a photograph of them,&nbsp;
and the resulting polaroid picture will reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:01.760
whatever their deepest desire happens to be&nbsp;
- whether it’s a trip to an amusement park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:06.080
a new tie, or to reconnect with&nbsp;
their estranged father, Keith.

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:10.720
Is it a little creepy to pry into someone’s most&nbsp;
private thoughts like this without them knowing?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:17.120
Absolutely. In fact, it’s super creepy. But hey,&nbsp;
what they don’t know won’t hurt them, right?

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:21.440
Maybe all this violating the privacy of your&nbsp;
closest loved ones has worked up a powerful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:26.320
thirst in you, but you don’t just want any&nbsp;
old cup of joe. Maybe you want to have the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:32.560
exact cup of coffee you had at a now-closed&nbsp;
diner in 1995. Or maybe you want to know what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:37.280
a liquid dream tastes like. Or perhaps you&nbsp;
just need a cup of antifreeze for your car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:42.000
and really don’t feel like going to the hardware&nbsp;
store to get some. If this describes you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:48.880
then you need to get your hands on SCP-294,&nbsp;
deceptively known as The Coffee Machine.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:53.360
We say “deceptively” because this anomaly&nbsp;
is so much more than a coffee machine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:57.120
With a little pocket change and the&nbsp;
electronic keypad connected to it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:02.960
you can order any liquid you desire, even things&nbsp;
that don’t traditionally come as liquids. No&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:09.200
matter your thirst, you can satisfy it with the&nbsp;
help of SCP-294. Of course, there is the possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:13.520
downside of ordering something dangerous or&nbsp;
deadly and then drinking it, but frankly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:19.120
that would be more your fault than SCP-294’s.&nbsp;
Remember to read the warning labels, kids.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:24.560
Maybe you’ve ordered an alien energy drink from&nbsp;
SCP-294, and it really isn’t sitting well with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:30.640
you. You can feel your liver withering away inside&nbsp;
you and even if you call an ambulance, you’re not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.640 --> 00:08:36.880
sure that it’ll get here in time to save you.&nbsp;
It’s starting to go dark - is this the end? No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:41.760
because lucky for you, you took&nbsp;
the time to acquire SCP-2295,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:47.280
also known as The Best Bear - a name that&nbsp;
this plush creature has more than earned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:51.920
You see, this bear is the world’s smallest&nbsp;
yet most competent trauma surgeon.

00:08:51.920 --> 00:08:57.280
If ever someone collapses with organ failure&nbsp;
within two meters of this magnanimous little bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.280 --> 00:09:01.760
it will create a perfect, functional organ&nbsp;
from nearby materials like yarn and string&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:07.600
to replace the broken one, and then perform a&nbsp;
flawless, life-saving surgery on its patients.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.600 --> 00:09:11.840
If ever you worry your organs are on the&nbsp;
fritz, then you’ll be glad that you can count&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:17.680
SCP-2295 among your personal possessions.&nbsp;
Also, even when your organs aren’t failing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:21.600
nobody can deny that it’s nice to have a&nbsp;
cute little teddy bear around to cuddle.

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:26.720
But what if you don’t want a little bear or a&nbsp;
magic butler to solve all of your problems? Maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.280
you want to be a little more self-sufficient,&nbsp;
and gain the knowledge and skills vital to live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:38.160
the life you want to live. If this applies&nbsp;
to you, then you’re going to adore SCP-5094,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:44.560
also known as Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse. This&nbsp;
software which comes on a CD-ROM is the ultimate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:50.240
find for the life-long learner! Anyone who has&nbsp;
the program can be personally tutored by Miss J,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:54.960
the perfect digital teacher, on almost&nbsp;
any subject they can possibly imagine.

00:09:54.960 --> 00:09:58.400
Want to become an expert in advanced&nbsp;
thermonuclear physics? Want to be able&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:02.720
to memorize every single one of Shakespeare’s&nbsp;
works to the letter? Want to know everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:08.240
a human being could possibly know about&nbsp;
cats? Have no fear, Miss J has your back!

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:14.400
With her trademark intensive courses, she can&nbsp;
turn novices into experts in just a few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:18.880
leaving you feeling enriched by the knowledge&nbsp;
you’ve just been exploring. If expanding your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:23.040
mind and your horizons on a regular basis&nbsp;
with the best teacher in the world sounds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:23.040 --> 00:10:30.000
like a dream come true to you, then SCP-5094 will&nbsp;
be an SCP object you’d kill to get your hands on.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:34.720
Metaphorically speaking, of course, Miss&nbsp;
J would never condone violence after all.

00:10:34.720 --> 00:10:39.200
After a hard day of hitting the books, or&nbsp;
computer screen, you’re going to need a snack.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:39.200 --> 00:10:45.840
But just not any snack. You want one that’s out of&nbsp;
this world, or maybe even out of this dimension.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.840 --> 00:10:52.480
It’s time to pay a visit to SCP-261, also&nbsp;
known as The Inter-Dimensional Vending Machine.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:57.520
This machine randomly generates exciting snacks&nbsp;
and drinks from all across the multiverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.520 --> 00:11:03.200
including Fruits of the Loom, a package of three&nbsp;
pieces of edible underwear in fun, bright colors,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:07.680
and Rat on a stick which is…&nbsp;
well, exactly what it sounds like.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:13.520
And finally, what do you get for the person&nbsp;
who has everything else? The best gift of all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:17.840
the gift… of life. There are still&nbsp;
plenty of diseases that even the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:22.880
SCP-Foundation has not been able to&nbsp;
cure, except with one extremely rare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:29.600
and extremely special anomalous item&nbsp;
- SCP-500. Also known as The Panacea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:35.360
the SCP is a bottle containing a small number of&nbsp;
pills capable of curing any ailment known to man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:43.360
from Alzheimer’s to the Flesh That Hates. When it&nbsp;
comes to healing, there is no equal to SCP-500.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:45.760
And considering you’ll be&nbsp;
drinking interdimensional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:48.960
soft drinks and eating truly&nbsp;
disgusting amounts of pizza,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.960 --> 00:11:53.200
it’s never a terrible idea to have a&nbsp;
cure for cardiac arrest laying around.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.400
And there you have it, folks! A list of the SCP&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.720
Objects you actually want. The hardest&nbsp;
part is going to be breaking into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.720 --> 00:12:04.560
heavily-guarded Foundation containment&nbsp;
sites to get them in the first place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:04.560 --> 00:12:09.520
but hey, we can cross that bridge when we get&nbsp;
to it. Which of these objects do you think are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:14.240
worth the risk of getting shot by a Mobile&nbsp;
Task Force for? Let us know in the comments!

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:20.880
Now go check out “The Eye Pods -&nbsp;
SCP-131” and “SCP-1609 - Remains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:25.520
of a Chair” for more SCP objects you&nbsp;
wouldn’t mind having in your life!

